      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging a bike transport service from Hyderabad to Udupi, it is essential to understand the statutory tax framework and insurance requirements that apply to the journey. The primary tax levied on such transport services is the Goods and Services Tax (GST).</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Depending on the nature of the service provider, the GST rate can be either the standard 18% or a reduced 5% rate for certain categories of vehicle transport services.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The 5% rate is typically applicable to services that fall under the “transport of goods” category, provided the service provider has registered under the GST regime and meets the necessary conditions.</span></li></ul>

<p>In addition to GST, transporters must also consider the cost of transit marine insurance, which protects the bike against loss or damage during the road journey. The insurance premium is calculated as a percentage of the declared value of the bike, usually ranging from 1.5% to 3%.</p>
<p>The exact percentage depends on the insurer’s underwriting guidelines, the distance, the mode of transport, and any additional risk mitigation measures such as GPS tracking or dedicated drivers.</p>

